  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/microphysogobio-tafangensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>This species originates from the southern Chinese province of Zhejiang, where it is endemic (i.e., seen worldwide, only there) in the system of the most important river of this province, the Qiantang.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/microphysogobio-tafangensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>This province is not located in the tropics, the climate is subtropical; in winter, temperatures drop to just below 10°C, in summer they rise to 30°C.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/microphysogobio-tafangensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Accordingly, one should not keep the fish too warm and especially at seasonally varying temperatures.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/microphysogobio-tafangensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>One should keep them, according to their origin, with good current and clear water; the bottom should be gritty-sandy.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/microphysogobio-tafangensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>They are peaceful among each other and against other fish.</p>"
    }
  ],
